      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Canonical product theory makes zeros a global divisor, whereas reverse Mellin mapping makes those locations candidate exponents in geometric averaging errors; the coefficient of each exponent is observable-dependent, and the theta example shows that spectral orthogonality can annihilate every such coefficient without removing the divisor.",
